content:
Help me define subdomains. Below I will provide the current state of the domain. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted domain objects and their associations:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Seller",
      "description": "Person offering an item for auction."
    },
    {
      "name": "Listing",
      "description": "Public posting that offers an item for auction.",
      "attributes": [
        "Item"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Item",
      "description": "Object being auctioned.",
      "attributes": [
        "Item Description"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Item Description",
      "description": "Details that describe the item."
    },
    {
      "name": "Bidder",
      "description": "Person placing bids on auctioned items."
    },
    {
      "name": "Bid",
      "description": "Offer from a bidder to purchase the item."
    },
    {
      "name": "Auction Manager",
      "description": "Person overseeing auction setup and bidding."
    },
    {
      "name": "Auction",
      "description": "Process in which bidders compete for the item.",
      "attributes": [
        "Item",
        "Scheduled Time",
        "Winner"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Scheduled Time",
      "description": "Planned start time of the auction."
    },
    {
      "name": "Winner",
      "description": "Bidder who wins the auction."
    },
    {
      "name": "Shipping Officer",
      "description": "Person coordinating delivery to the winner."
    },
    {
      "name": "Delivery",
      "description": "Transfer of the sold item to the winning bidder.",
      "attributes": [
        "Item",
        "Winner"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
{
  "associations": [
    {
      "from": "Seller",
      "to": "Listing",
      "description": "Seller creates the listing."
    },
    {
      "from": "Seller",
      "to": "Item",
      "description": "Seller provides the item."
    },
    {
      "from": "Auction Manager",
      "to": "Listing",
      "description": "Auction Manager reviews the listing."
    },
    {
      "from": "Auction Manager",
      "to": "Auction",
      "description": "Auction Manager manages the auction."
    },
    {
      "from": "Bidder",
      "to": "Listing",
      "description": "Bidder views the listing."
    },
    {
      "from": "Bidder",
      "to": "Bid",
      "description": "Bidder submits a bid."
    },
    {
      "from": "Auction Manager",
      "to": "Bid",
      "description": "Auction Manager monitors the bid."
    },
    {
      "from": "Shipping Officer",
      "to": "Delivery",
      "description": "Shipping Officer performs the delivery."
    },
    {
      "from": "Delivery",
      "to": "Bidder",
      "description": "Delivery is handed to the bidder."
    }
  ]
}
```

#### Task:
- Group these objects by domain concerns. 
- Find a name for the subdomain then list the objects that belong to it. 
- Return the subdomains in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "...": {
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Here are the subdomains:
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Item Listing": {
      "objects": [
        "Seller",
        "Listing",
        "Item",
        "Item Description"
      ]
    },
    "Auctioning": {
      "objects": [
        "Bidder",
        "Auction Manger",
        "Bid",
        "Auction",
        "Item",
        "Scheduled Time",
        "Winner"
      ]
    },
    "Item Delivery": {
      "objects": [
        "Shipping Officer",
        "Delivery",
        "Item",
        "Winner"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```
